> the card-present check beside it is an inventory, and on this card it DOES run, since it is gated on `failed_count > 0` and **every block here fails**

Every block's *write* fails. That is not the same as counting as a failure. `:984-987`:

```c
if(!iso15693_poller_block_is_empty(remaining, size)) {
    instance->clone_failed_count++;
    iso15693_poller_mark_failed(instance, block);
}
```

A refused write whose block reads back EMPTY increments nothing. So the card described two lines up - "refuses every write, answers a read at every address" - ends with `failed_count == 0` whenever its blocks already read as zeros, and the gate at `:1160` is false. The inventory does not run.

Only a cost estimate, so nothing downstream moves, but the "since" does not hold in general. "on a card whose blocks still hold data" would.
